  "question": {
    "text": "Let the circles $C_1:(x-\\alpha)^2+(y-\\beta)^2=r_1^2$ and $C_2:(x-8)^2+\\left(y-\\frac{15}{2}\\right)^2=r_2^2$ touch each other externally at the point $(6,6)$. If the point $(6,6)$ divides the line segment joining the centres of the circles $C_1$ and $C_2$ internally in the ratio $2: 1$, then $(\\alpha+\\beta)+4\\left(r_1^2+r_2^2\\right)$ equals",
